<p>
   The Code 93 barcode is a high-density linear barcode symbology that can encode a wide range of characters, including uppercase letters (A-Z), numbers (0-9), and a variety of special characters. It is commonly used in applications where space is limited, such as on small labels or packaging.
   It is an enhanced version of the Code 39 barcode, offering improved data density and error correction capabilities. The Code 93 symbology includes a checksum character that helps ensure data integrity during scanning, making it more reliable for applications that require accurate data capture.
   You can use the extended code93 to encode all the ASCII characters by setting the <code>IsExtended</code> parameter to true.
   You can change the height and width of the bars by setting the <code>ModuleHeight</code> and <code>ModuleWidth</code> parameters respectively.
   You can show the text below the barcode by setting the <code>ShowText</code> parameter to true.
   You can use the <code>Code93Symbology</code> component to generate Code 93 barcodes in your application.
</p>


<div style="height: 400px">
    <FluentStack Height="100%" VerticalGap="50" Orientation="Orientation.Vertical">
        <FluentStack HorizontalGap="8px">
            <FluentTextInput Immediate
                             Label="Value to encode as barcode"
                             @bind-Value="Value" />
        </FluentStack>
        
        <FluentCxBarcode Value="@Value">
            <Code93Symbology />
        </FluentCxBarcode>
    </FluentStack>
</div>

@code {
    private string Value { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
